WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.400
the restored Colonial Village of Williamsburg&nbsp;
Virginia even in the earliest days of our nation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.610
the druggists mortar and pestle was a proud&nbsp;
symbol of reliability but how reliable where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:22.620
the concoctions assembled by the pharmacist to&nbsp;
that area from a weird collection of herbs roots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:29.340
and other medications whose use was dictated&nbsp;
more by tradition than sound authority how pure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:35.040
uniform and stable were they and how much&nbsp;
laborious work went into their preparation

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:43.690
the conscientious apothecary of days gone by&nbsp;
did his best to fill the doctor's prescription&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:49.270
to the letter but he had no control over the&nbsp;
deterioration of his chemicals no proper way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:54.550
of blending them no means for testing their&nbsp;
strength it's little wonder that on some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.550 --> 00:01:00.580
occasions the remedy did more damage than the&nbsp;
ailment it was intended to cure wonderful to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:05.440
look back into the past like this but as so&nbsp;
often happens we find on closer inspection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:12.220
that the good old days weren't quite as good as we&nbsp;
imagine today for example the pharmacist commands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:17.980
the resources of America's great drug industry&nbsp;
for example firms like Rexall drug company in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:23.800
whose Los Angeles laboratories we find scientists&nbsp;
constantly improving on old established products&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:28.900
and constantly seeking new practical uses for&nbsp;
the discoveries of the research scientists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:36.010
samples produced in the laboratories pilot plant&nbsp;
are stored for long periods under all sorts of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:40.870
temperatures and humidity then are analyzed&nbsp;
to determine if any change has taken place

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:50.280
the mortar and pestle are still in&nbsp;
use in this case tablets are ground&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.260
up before going through any number of analyses

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:04.080
first the samples are weighed on an&nbsp;
analytical balance scales so sensitive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.040
they can tell the weight of an eyelash&nbsp;
or your signature on a piece of paper

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:19.600
they have the most uncanny ways of determining&nbsp;
the exact chemical and physical makeup of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.180
drug for example if they want to find the&nbsp;
amount of vitamin b12 it contains they add&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:30.760
microorganisms that require that vitamin for&nbsp;
growth as the bugs developed they cause the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:36.430
liquid to become cloudy when all the vitamin&nbsp;
is consumed the microorganism stops growing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:43.540
the degree of cloudiness reveals the potency&nbsp;
of the vitamin various elements are known to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:49.150
absorb a precise amount of infrared light rays&nbsp;
so they passed such rays through a sample and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:54.190
the rays that are not absorbed are recorded on a&nbsp;
graph revealing exactly the nature of the sample

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:06.530
we take our drugstores pretty much for&nbsp;
granted but to many of the residents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:11.450
of 17th century Williamsburg a store like&nbsp;
this when it spells the difference between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.920
life and death come to think of it&nbsp;
I guess it smells the same to us

